  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "New benchmarks test temporal and interventional causal discovery on kinetic models and CRISPR data, exposing method limits under partial observability.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is head-to-head evaluation of existing causal discovery methods on biological networks. A bioRxiv preprint compares temporal approaches (tMIIC, PCMCI+/LPCMCI, SVAR-FCI) on simulated biochemical kinetic models, with fully and partially observed settings that include latent confounders and unobserved variables. A published study compares interventional causal structure learning algorithms on synthetic and CRISPR perturbation data for gene regulatory network inference. The emphasis is on assessing methods under partial observability and with interventional data rather than proposing new algorithms. Two further items, hierarchical dynamical surrogates of trust-game decisions and ODE-based reconstruction of hidden epidemic states with multi-agent reinforcement learning, share a theme of inference from incomplete observations but do not address causal network benchmarking.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
